; A keep in the middle, two flanking bastions outboard, and a breakable wall
; sealing each side of the keep (issue #54, part from #53). All four stand
; at the same height, y=300, so the wall is the only thing that makes one
; side of the keep different from the other.
;
; The keep starts as a shelter. Both walls open at full HP (~three solid
; pickaxe strikes each, `BreakableWall.hp`'s own default), standing 140 px
; tall right at the keep's edge -- taller than a body is wide, so nothing
; hit toward either side of the keep bounces off the wall and stays put
; instead of ringing out. The bastions are not sheltered: their outer edges
; are open sky straight down to the kill zone, the same as any flat stage's
; ends, so `every_stage_can_ring_out` has its route from round one without
; needing a wall touched. What the wall changes is the *keep*: while it
; stands, a hit toward either edge is a hit that stops there; once it goes,
; that edge is a ring-out lane that was not open a moment before -- breaking
; one wall hands the other player's spot a new way to lose the round, aimed
; back at whoever is standing in the keep when it happens.
;
; Nothing here needs the wall broken to be crossed, though, per
; `BreakableWall.gd`'s own header: only a fast swing damages it, so it can be
; "leaned on, planted on and climbed" for free. From the keep's edge a
; standing player's head is about 116 px from the wall's near top corner --
; comfortably inside pickaxe reach (~150) and reachable by the sword's blade
; too, so the wall is climbed with modest skill from that side, no different
; from any staircase ledge elsewhere in the rotation. From a bastion it is a
; 124 px gap to the wall's far face (inside the 100-180 px this rotation
; already asks a pickaxe to fling) and then about 153 px up to the same top
; corner -- right at a pickaxe's reach and a two-part climb (fling the gap,
; then hook the face) for the sword and dagger "with effort," never a single
; impossible reach. The staff clears the whole thing, gap and wall, in one
; plant from the bastion. So the keep is a shelter you can still visit
; without breaking anything, at the cost of climbing in over the top while
; whoever holds it gets a free swing at you -- and it is a shelter an
; attacker can instead spend three solid hits to remove permanently, opening
; a straight line to the drop for the rest of the round.
;
; The rising kill zone (ADR-0012) only has to climb 230 px here -- from
; y=480 to the shared y=250 every spawn drops onto -- since keep and
; bastions share one height. Once it reaches that line every surface goes
; under together; nobody is sheltered from the lava by anything, wall or no
; wall, and there is no pocket underneath any of the three platforms for it
; to trap someone in -- each is a floating slab with open air below, same as
; every other stage's floors.

; Backdrop (issue #117): fortress.
